heights and the final comparison","The cutoff and polynomial size",1]],"used_by_total":7},"results":[{"id":"syntax/language/formula-compilation","title":"Formulas and their polynomial compilation","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.Syntax.Formula, ZInQ.Syntax.Formula.compile, ZInQ.Syntax.Formula.Holds, ZInQ.Syntax.Build, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.fresh, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.call, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.rational, ZInQ.Syntax.globalEq, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.template, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.fullFormula, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.template_eq, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.nz, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.pos","summary":"Formulas. A formula over $\\mathbb Z[X_i:i\\in\\mathbb N]$ is built from atoms $a\\doteq b$ ($a,b$ polynomials), $\\langle f\\rangle$ ($f$ a polynomial) and call atoms $\\langle\\tau[g;w]\\rangle$ ($\\tau$ an existential polynomial with $p$ parameters and $m$ witnesses, $g$ a $p$-tuple of polynomials, $w\\in\\mathbb N$ the witness start) by the connectives $\\bigwedge(\\varphi_1,\\dots,\\varphi_k)$ and…","route":"../roadmap/syntax/language/index.html#formula-compilation"},{"id":"syntax/language/builder-soundness","title":"Template construction from formulas","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Syntax.Build.Allocates, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.Allocates.bind, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.template_construction","summary":"Call a construction *allocating* if, run from any counter and list of global equations, it never decreases the counter and only appends global equations $q\\,X_c\\doteq u$ whose variables $c$ are newly allocated (at least the initial and below the final counter), in increasing order. Every fresh variable, call, rational constant and gadget is allocating, and so is every construction composed of them.","route":"../roadmap/syntax/language/index.html#builder-soundness"},{"id":"syntax/language/builder-well-formed","title":"Witness scope of constructed templates and recipes","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Syntax.Formula.InScope, ZInQ.Syntax.ExPoly.WitnessScope, ZInQ.Syntax.ExPoly.WitnessScope.rel_iff, ZInQ.Syntax.ExPoly.WitnessScope.wf, ZInQ.Syntax.Build.Facts.witnessScope, ZInQ.Syntax.templateLibrary_witnessScope, ZInQ.Syntax.CompositionRecipe.witnessScope_of, ZInQ.Syntax.closeRecipe_callBlocks_disjoint, ZInQ.Syntax.mainRecipe_callBlocks_disjoint, ZInQ.Syntax.valueUnionRecipe_callBlocks_disjoint, ZInQ.Syntax.valueRecipe_callBlocks_disjoint, ZInQ.Syntax.integersRecipe_callBlocks_disjoint, ZInQ.Syntax.translate_witnessScope, ZInQ.Syntax.specLib_witnessScope, ZInQ.Syntax.specLib_precisionCircuit_witnessScope","summary":"Call an existential polynomial $\\tau$ with $p$ parameters and $v$ variables *in scope* if $[\\![\\tau]\\!]=\\kappa(\\varphi)$ for a formula $\\varphi$ such that","route":"../roadmap/syntax/language/index.html#builder-well-formed"},{"id":"syntax/language/call-semantics","title":"Evaluation of a template call","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Syntax.ev_callPoly, ZInQ.Syntax.ExPoly.exists_blockUpdate_call_iff","summary":"Let $\\tau$ be a template or recipe with $p$ parameters, $v$ variables and $m=v-p$ witnesses, all of whose variables have index below $v$. Let $g_0,\\dots,g_{p-1}$ be polynomials, $w\\in\\mathbb N$ and $x:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb Q$. Then Consequently, if none of the variables $X_w,\\dots,X_{w+m-1}$ occurs in any $g_i$, then for every assignment $x$ of the remaining variables \\iff\\mathrm{Rel}_\\tau(g_0(x),\\dots,g_{p-1}(x)).$$","route":"../roadmap/syntax/language/index.html#call-semantics"},{"id":"syntax/language/existential-lifting","title":"Private witness blocks","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.Syntax.Formula.exists_blocks_iff","summary":"Let $\\varphi$ be a formula whose atoms of the form $\\langle\\cdot\\rangle$ are calls $\\langle\\tau_i[g_i;w_i]\\rangle$, $i=1,\\dots,k$, where $\\tau_i$ has $p_i$ parameters, $v_i$ variables, $m_i=v_i-p_i$ witnesses and all its variables below $v_i$. Put $B_i=\\{w_i,\\dots,w_i+m_i-1\\}$ and 